BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7b480d1b8d69dcbd@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261123T223222Z
DTSTART:20261201T203000Z
DTEND:20261201T213000Z
SUMMARY:Kids STEAM: DIY Puzzles
LOCATION:Kay Fox Room
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/18065787
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Kids STEAM has a new day of the week while Miss Scout is out. 
 But join Parker for plenty of activities each month!\n\nMake your own puzz
 le out of upcycled calendars! Try out the laminator and die cut machine fr
 om our Makerspace\, and learn to make your own paper box to hold your puzz
 le pieces.\n\nRegistration required. \n\nFor ages 6 - 11 and their caregiv
 ers.\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:335a4b44d52560d1@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261123T223222Z
DTSTART:20261202T170000Z
DTEND:20261202T220000Z
SUMMARY:American Red Cross Blood Drive
LOCATION:Heberton Hall
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17124292
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Join KPL and the Red Cross for a winter blood drive! Consider 
 donating blood to help others in need. Please call 1-800-RED CROSS (1-800-
 733-2767) or visit RedCrossBlood.org and enter: KEENE to schedule an appoi
 ntment. Maximize your blood donation and help more patients. If you are an
  eligible type O\, B - or A - donor\, consider making a Power Red donation
 . Red blood cells are the most commonly transfused blood component. Stream
 line your donation experience and save up to 15 minutes by visiting RedCro
 ssBlood.org/RapidPass to complete your pre-donation reading and health his
 tory questions on the day of your appointment.\nSource: Keene Public Libra
 ry
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b5dd723d164bd0b0@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261123T223222Z
DTSTART:20261202T200000Z
DTEND:20261202T210000Z
SUMMARY:KPL Trustees Fine Art Cttee
LOCATION:Miller-Vincent Room
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/16292147
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Source: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1429a5a931bbeabd@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261123T223222Z
DTSTART:20261202T223000Z
DTEND:20261203T003000Z
SUMMARY:Sublimation printing
LOCATION:Kingsbury Makerspace
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17565375
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Come learn about sublimation printing using our Epson sublimat
 ion printer. You will learn by making one custom designed porcelain mug.  
 All materials are provided. Please come with a design in mind or better ye
 t a digital file.  If you are not already a member of the Kingsbury Makers
 pace please complete the Introduction to the Makerspace tutorial before at
 tending this workshop.\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2cc2538a1c507dfd@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261123T223222Z
DTSTART:20261203T230000Z
DTEND:20261204T000000Z
SUMMARY:Bonnie Tomlinson Author and Home Organizer
LOCATION:Ruth Huntress Auditorium
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17645602
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Bonnie Borromeo Tomlinson is the author of STEP BUYING BINS an
 d other blunt but practical advice\, STOP PUSHING PERFECTION and just crea
 te a home you can actually keep neat\, and the newly published YOU DON'T N
 EED IT and other advice about setting up your first home. Bonnie will pres
 ent on topics such as downsizing\, profiting from castoffs\, creating orga
 nizing systems\, over-shopping and using what you have on hand and most of
  all how to live an organized life that doesn't involve constant maintenan
 ce. You can check out copies of her books here at the library.\nSource: Ke
 ene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:869422db0133f789@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261123T223222Z
DTSTART:20261205T160000Z
DTEND:20261205T190000Z
SUMMARY:Friends of KPL Pop-Up Sale
LOCATION:Circulation Lobby
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/18028917
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Shop for your next cozy evening read or holiday gifts\, all wh
 ile supporting programming at your local library! The Friends of KPL are h
 osting a pop-up sale for childrens books in our Winter Street lobby! Stop 
 by to snag a book or five at great prices. All books are donated to the Fr
 iends of KPL and range from like-new to gently used condition and all prof
 its support the library and library programming.\nSource: Keene Public Lib
 rary
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:014cc541a00f3be9@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261123T223222Z
DTSTART:20261205T180000Z
DTEND:20261205T200000Z
SUMMARY:Holiday Tea - Celebrate the Winter Solstice
LOCATION:Heberton Hall\, Heberton Hall Kitchen
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17091130
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the Winter Solstice at Keene Public Library’s Annu
 al Tea Party on Saturday\, December 5\, 2026\, from 1–3 pm ! Join us for
  a special presentation about America's Stonehenge. Learn about the histor
 y\, traditions\, and wonders of the Winter Solstice. Gather with friends\,
  sip something warm\, enjoy delicious goodies\, and welcome the winter sea
 son with an afternoon of warmth\, wonder\, and discovery!\n\nRegistration 
 is required. For more information please email Amy akraemer@keenenh.gov or
  call 603 352-0157\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:033b0a1b3bb634c4@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261123T223222Z
DTSTART:20261207T160000Z
DTEND:20261207T180000Z
SUMMARY:Community Resources: Monadnock Peer Support
LOCATION:Circulation Lobby
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/18016658
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Get information and connect with services through Monadnock Pe
 er Support for recovery services\, mental health and wellness.\n\nMPS is a
  member-driven organization that establishes a culture in which our member
 s and participants feel more empowered to get support from and give suppor
 t to peers. We provide many free services including 30  support groups wee
 kly\, meals\, field trips\, respite stays and more! Visit https://www.mona
 dnockpsa.org/ for more information or chat with a member during tabling.\n
 Source: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
