BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:265e10e50b45f944@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261123T223222Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261201T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261201T150000
SUMMARY:World AIDS DAY - Quilt Panel Display
LOCATION:Main Reading Room
URL:https://brookslibraryvt.org/event/world-aids-day/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Brooks Memorial Library
DESCRIPTION:All are welcome to join The AIDS Project of Southern Vermont w
 ho will commemorate World AIDS Day on Tuesday\, December 1st\, with two ev
 ents in Brattleboro. Brooks Memorial Library is honored to host an AIDS Me
 morial Quilt panel\, including a panel from the CALL MY NAME initiative ho
 noring Black and Brown lives lost to HIV/AIDS\, with outreach and educatio
 nal resources available from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m. in the Main Reading Room\, 
 The Quilt will remain on display through December 5th. \nThat evening\, th
 e Latchis Theatre will display Quilt panels beginning at 6:30 p.m.\, follo
 wed by a 7 p.m. screening of the award-winning documentary Common Threads:
  Stories from the Quilt. The screening – by donation – will benefit th
 e AIDS Project of Southern Vermont\, with 50% of proceeds donated to suppo
 rt its work. All are welcome to join in remembrance\, education\, and comm
 unity connection.\nSource: Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
