DESCRIPTION:The Women’s Freedom Center is hosting a Femmes and Thems
  Collage Club for survivors of Intimate Partner Violence\, Sexual Violen
 ce and their Allies on the first Friday of every month from 1:30PM- 3PM at
  Brooks Memorial Library in the Community Room on the third floor. We have
  supplies galore and good conversation. Bring your own collage materials\,
  or just yourself.\nSource: Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b6b88171b7114198@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261123T223222Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T160000
SUMMARY:Meet the Judges: Brattleboro Festival of Miniatures
LOCATION:Main Reading Room
URL:https://brookslibraryvt.org/event/meet-the-judges-brattleboro-festival
 -of-miniatures/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Brooks Memorial Library
DESCRIPTION:What qualifies a person to judge a miniature window contest? W
 hat are the criteria for judging? Are they miniature judges or judges of m
 iniatures? \nMeet these magnificent (life-size) miniaturists at this Bratt
 leboro Festival of Miniatures event – Becky Gannon\, Julie Steiner\, Nat
 asha Sawyer\, and Carinne Gee. They will share a little about their miniat
 ures journeys and explain some of the criteria they used to judge the near
 ly 100 window scenes around Brattleboro. Save the date now for this rare o
 pportunity to meet four giants in the mini world. See you there!\nSource: 
 Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
